<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal supplementary 1996 budget boosts health.</title>
<headline>Portugal supplementary 1996 budget boosts health.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese government's supplementary budget for 1996, approved by the cabinet on Thursday, will inject 24 billion escudos to the health ministry, a government spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;Health is the only area that will be reinforced by the supplementary budget,&quot; Vitalino Canas told reporters after the weekly cabinet meeting.</p>
<p>As Prime Minister Antonio Guterres said earlier this week, the 1996 supplementary budget forecasts that the budget deficit would stand at 4.0 percent at the end of 1996, down from an earlier forecast of 4.2 percent.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
